DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ccoonnffssttrr() gets the value of configuration‐dependent string variables.

       The  _n_a_m_e argument is the system variable to be queried.  The following
       variables are supported:

       __CCSS__GGNNUU__LLIIBBCC__VVEERRSSIIOONN (GNU C library only; since glibc 2.3.2)
              A string which identifies the GNU C library version on this sys‐
              tem (e.g., "glibc 2.3.4").

       __CCSS__GGNNUU__LLIIBBPPTTHHRREEAADD__VVEERRSSIIOONN (GNU C library only; since glibc 2.3.2)
              A string which identifies the POSIX implementation  supplied  by
              this C library (e.g., "NPTL 2.3.4" or "linuxthreads-0.10").

       __CCSS__PPAATTHH
              A  value  for  the  PPAATTHH  variable which indicates where all the
              POSIX.2 standard utilities can be found.

       If _b_u_f is not NULL and _s_i_z_e is not zero, ccoonnffssttrr() copies the value  of
       the string to _b_u_f truncated to _s_i_z_e _- _1 bytes if necessary, with a null
       byte  ('\0')  as terminator.  This can be detected by comparing the re‐
       turn value of ccoonnffssttrr() against _s_i_z_e.

       If _s_i_z_e is zero and _b_u_f is NULL, ccoonnffssttrr() just returns  the  value  as
       defined below.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       If _n_a_m_e is a valid configuration variable, ccoonnffssttrr() returns the number
       of  bytes  (including the terminating null byte) that would be required
       to hold the entire value of that variable.  This value may  be  greater
       than _s_i_z_e, which means that the value in _b_u_f is truncated.

       If  _n_a_m_e  is a valid configuration variable, but that variable does not
       have a value, then ccoonnffssttrr() returns 0.  If _n_a_m_e does not correspond to
       a valid configuration variable, ccoonnffssttrr() returns 0, and _e_r_r_n_o  is  set
       to EEIINNVVAALL.

